(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["anatomy-exam-3-endocrine-quiz-version-6"]={"title":"Endocrine System — Anatomy Exam 3 (Set 6)","category":"Anatomy","questions":[{"q":"The pituitary gland measures approximately how much in transverse diameter?","choices":["30 mm","12 mm","6 mm","20 mm"],"answer":1,"exp":"The pituitary gland is described as a reddish-grey, ovoid body about 12 mm in transverse diameter. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 13"},{"q":"The pituitary gland measures approximately how much in anteroposterior diameter?","choices":["4 mm","8 mm","16 mm","12 mm"],"answer":1,"exp":"The pituitary gland measures about 8 mm in anteroposterior diameter, smaller than its 12 mm transverse diameter. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 13"},{"q":"The pituitary gland weighs approximately how much?","choices":["1000 mg","50 mg","500 mg","250 mg"],"answer":2,"exp":"The pituitary gland weighs approximately 500 mg. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 13"},{"q":"Inferiorly and anteriorly, the pituitary gland is related to which air-filled space?","choices":["Mastoid air cells","Sphenoid air sinus","Ethmoid air cells","Frontal air sinus"],"answer":1,"exp":"Inferiorly and anteriorly, the pituitary gland is related to the sphenoid air sinus. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 13"},{"q":"The pituitary gland is related behind (posteriorly) to which bony structure?","choices":["Foramen magnum","Crista galli","Clivus","Dorsum sellae"],"answer":3,"exp":"The pituitary gland is related behind to the dorsum sellae. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 13"},{"q":"The diaphragma sellae, which covers the pituitary gland superiorly, is composed of which tissue?","choices":["Periosteum only","Pia mater","Arachnoid mater","Dura mater"],"answer":3,"exp":"The diaphragma sellae is a fold of dura mater covering the pituitary gland superiorly, pierced centrally by the infundibulum. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 13"},{"q":"In the pars distalis, chromophobe cells make up approximately what fraction of the cells and characteristically lack cytoplasmic granules?","choices":["50%","75%","10%","25%"],"answer":0,"exp":"Chromophobes make up about 50% of pars distalis cells and lack granules in their cytoplasm. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 21"},{"q":"In the pars distalis, chromophil cells (which contain cytoplasmic granules and are larger than chromophobes) make up approximately what fraction of the cells?","choices":["50%","90%","10%","25%"],"answer":0,"exp":"Chromophils, which contain granules, make up about 50% of pars distalis cells (split into acidophils and basophils). — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 21"},{"q":"Basophils of the pars distalis, which have bluish cytoplasm, make up approximately what percentage of anterior pituitary cells?","choices":["40%","10%","70%","50%"],"answer":0,"exp":"Basophils make up about 40% of the cells of the pars distalis and secrete TSH, ACTH, FSH, and LH. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 21"},{"q":"Compared to acidophils, basophils of the anterior pituitary are generally described as:","choices":["Identical in size and staining","Found only in the posterior lobe","Larger and stain deeper","Smaller and lighter staining"],"answer":2,"exp":"Basophils are generally larger in size and stain more deeply than acidophils. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 21"},{"q":"Within the pars nervosa, the homogenous intercellular substance that precipitates on fixation to form a distinctive structure is called a:","choices":["Negri body","Nissl body","Herring body","Barr body"],"answer":2,"exp":"On fixation, the homogenous intercellular substance in the pars nervosa precipitates to form Herring's body. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 22"},{"q":"The bundles of nerve fibers in the pars nervosa arise in the hypothalamus and descend to the posterior lobe, forming which named tract?","choices":["Spinothalamic sensory tract","Hypothalamo-hypophyseal tract","Corticospinal motor tract","Mammillothalamic fiber tract"],"answer":1,"exp":"These fibers form the hypothalamo-hypophyseal tract (HHT), descending from the hypothalamus to the pars nervosa. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 22"},{"q":"Each lobe of the thyroid gland measures approximately what dimensions (length x width x thickness)?","choices":["2 x 1 x 1 cm","10 x 6 x 4 cm","5 x 3 x 2 cm","8 x 5 x 3 cm"],"answer":2,"exp":"Each thyroid lobe is approximately 5 x 3 x 2 cm (length x width x thickness). — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 25"},{"q":"The thyroid isthmus measures approximately what dimensions (length x width)?","choices":["1.25 x 1.25 cm","2.5 cm x 2.0 cm","0.5 cm x 0.5 cm","4.0 cm x 3.5 cm"],"answer":0,"exp":"The thyroid isthmus measures approximately 1.25 x 1.25 cm. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 29"},{"q":"An occasional conical pyramidal lobe of the thyroid, usually present toward the left, connects to the hyoid bone via a fibrous or fibromuscular cord known as the:","choices":["Suspensory ligament of Berry","Sternothyroid muscle band","Levator glandulae thyroideae","Thyrohyoid membrane fibers"],"answer":2,"exp":"The pyramidal lobe connects to the hyoid bone via the levator glandulae thyroideae, a fibrous or fibromuscular cord. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 29"},{"q":"The apex of each thyroid lobe lies at the level of which laryngeal landmark?","choices":["The lower border of the cricoid cartilage","The oblique line of the thyroid cartilage","The greater cornu of the hyoid bone","The apex of the arytenoid cartilage"],"answer":1,"exp":"The apex of each thyroid lobe is at the level of the oblique line of the thyroid cartilage of the larynx. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 25"},{"q":"The base of each thyroid lobe lies at the level of which tracheal ring(s)?","choices":["6th or 7th","2nd or 3rd","4th or 5th","1st or 2nd"],"answer":2,"exp":"The base of each thyroid lobe lies at the level of the 4th or 5th tracheal ring. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 25"},{"q":"The thyroid gland spans which cervical-to-thoracic vertebral levels in the lower neck?","choices":["C3 to C5","C1 to C3","T2 to T4","C5 to T1"],"answer":3,"exp":"The thyroid gland lies in the lower part of the neck at the level of the 5th cervical (C5) to the 1st thoracic (T1) vertebrae. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 25"},{"q":"The superior and middle thyroid veins usually drain into which vein?","choices":["Internal jugular vein","External jugular vein","Brachiocephalic vein directly","Subclavian vein"],"answer":0,"exp":"The superior and middle thyroid veins usually end in the internal jugular vein. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 33"},{"q":"Lymphatic drainage of the thyroid gland is directed to paratracheal nodes and to deep cervical nodes located inferior to which muscle?","choices":["Sternocleidomastoid","Omohyoid","Thyrohyoid","Digastric"],"answer":1,"exp":"Thyroid lymphatics drain to deep cervical nodes inferior to the omohyoid muscle, along the internal jugular vein. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 33"},{"q":"Thyroid lymph vessels found in the interlobular connective tissue between lobes ultimately terminate in which ducts?","choices":["Cisterna chyli by direct drainage","The right lymphatic duct exclusively","Thoracic duct and right lymphatic duct","The thoracic duct exclusively"],"answer":2,"exp":"Interlobular thyroid lymph vessels terminate in both the thoracic duct and the right lymphatic duct. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 36"},{"q":"Autonomic innervation of the thyroid gland arises from the cervical portion of the sympathetic trunk and parasympathetic fibers from which cranial nerve?","choices":["Cranial nerve VII (facial)","Cranial nerve X (vagus)","Cranial nerve IX branches","Cranial nerve XII (hypoglossal)"],"answer":1,"exp":"Parasympathetic innervation of the thyroid arises from the vagus nerve (cranial nerve X). — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 36"},{"q":"Within the carotid sheath bordering the thyroid gland, which structure has the greater diameter, the internal jugular vein or the common/internal carotid artery?","choices":["Neither is part of the carotid sheath","They are equal in diameter","The carotid artery","The internal jugular vein"],"answer":3,"exp":"Within the carotid sheath, the jugular vein has a greater diameter than the carotid artery, and lies lateral to it. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 38"},{"q":"Each parathyroid gland typically measures approximately what dimensions?","choices":["15 x 8 x 4 mm","2 x 1 x 0.5 mm","25 x 15 x 8 mm","6 x 3 x 1 mm"],"answer":3,"exp":"Each parathyroid gland is commonly about 6 x 3 x 1 mm. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 44"},{"q":"Each parathyroid gland weighs approximately how much?","choices":["5 mg","50 mg","500 mg","150 mg"],"answer":1,"exp":"Each parathyroid gland weighs approximately 50 mg. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 44"},{"q":"Parathyroid glands are described in the lecture as having which color?","choices":["Bright reddish-tan","Pale ivory-white","Yellowish-brown","Bluish-grey mottled"],"answer":2,"exp":"The parathyroid glands are described as small, yellowish-brown, ovoid or lentiform structures. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 44"},{"q":"Which pair of parathyroid glands is more constant in location, usually lying midway along the posterior thyroid borders?","choices":["The superior parathyroid glands","Neither pair has a constant location","Both pairs equally","The inferior parathyroid glands"],"answer":0,"exp":"The superior parathyroid glands are more constant in location than the inferior glands. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 44"},{"q":"The inferior parathyroid glands may be found in the thyroid gland near which region?","choices":["Its base","The apex","The isthmus","The pyramidal lobe"],"answer":0,"exp":"The inferior parathyroid glands may sometimes be found in the thyroid gland near its base. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 44"},{"q":"The parathyroid glands lie in close proximity to the tracheoesophageal groove and which paired neck muscles?","choices":["Longus colli muscles","Digastric muscles","Sternocleidomastoid muscles","Scalene muscles"],"answer":0,"exp":"The parathyroid glands lie close to the tracheoesophageal groove and the longus colli muscles. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 47"},{"q":"Aberrant parathyroid glands may sometimes be found lying between the trachea and which structure?","choices":["The thyroid","The larynx","The esophagus","The carotid sheath"],"answer":0,"exp":"Aberrant parathyroid glands may lie between the trachea and the thyroid. — Endocrine for Posting.pptx, Slide 47"}]};
